  "authenticated_goals": [
    {
      "acceptance": "The independent suite covers every public behavior below, so no requirement is dropped: approval.review successfully transitions a DRAFT content revision to REVIEW status; approval.approve successfully transitions a REVIEWED content revision to APPROVED status only if all linked claims are SUPPORTED and media is valid/present; approval.status correctly reports the current status (DRAFT, REVIEW, APPROVED) for a given content ID; approval.approve raises ValueError if the content has not been reviewed; approval.approve raises ValueError if any linked claim is UNSUPPORTED, STALE, or CONFLICT; approval.approve raises ValueError if referenced media is missing or invalid; a content.edit operation (from M5) resets the approval status of the new revision to DRAFT, leaving old approvals historical; approval operations enforce project isolation (cannot access/approve content from other projects); approval data persists after the Python process exits and is reloaded in a new process using the same data_dir; invalid inputs, unknown IDs, and unsupported operations raise ValueError.",
