            "concurrency": "Single-threaded assumption per data_dir for this milestone. File system operations should use atomic writes where possible to prevent corruption during simple sequential usage.",
            "edge_behavior": "The module exposes MILESTONE_ID as 'M6' and handle(data_dir, request). It supports operations: approval.review(project_id, content_id), approval.approve(project_id, content_id), approval.status(project_id, content_id).\n\napproval.review marks the current revision of a content item as REVIEWED. Returns {content_id, revision, status: 'REVIEW'}.\n\napproval.approve validates that the current revision has been reviewed, all associated claims are currently SUPPORTED (via M3 logic), and all referenced media assets are present/valid (media list can be empty before M11). If valid, it marks the current revision as APPROVED. Returns {content_id, revision, status: 'APPROVED'}. Raises ValueError if not reviewed, claims unsupported/stale/conflicting, or media missing.\n\napproval.status returns the current approval state for the specified content ID. Returns {content_id, revision, status} where status is one of DRAFT, REVIEW, APPROVED. \n\nA semantic content.edit (from M5) resets the approval status of the new revision to DRAFT. Old approvals remain historical but do not authorize new content. Invalid input, unknown IDs, cross-project access, and unsupported operations raise ValueError. No success-shaped error objects. Persistence survives process restarts.",
